1
00:01:41,789 --> 00:01:49,030
[Genius Girlfriend]

2
00:01:49,289 --> 00:01:51,920
[Episode 6]

3
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:21,400
You really need to change this habit

4
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:24,170
of walking away while someone is talking.

5
00:02:27,310 --> 00:02:28,190
But it's good

6
00:02:29,630 --> 00:02:31,090
that you knew to come home.

7
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:34,280
If one day you really run away,

8
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:36,120
what should I do?

9
00:02:37,430 --> 00:02:38,760
Wouldn't that be great?

10
00:02:39,030 --> 00:02:41,430
You wouldn't have to see me
and get annoyed.

11
00:02:44,710 --> 00:02:45,500
Just now,

12
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:46,840
on my way back,

13
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:49,610
I actually passed by my old normal school.

14
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:52,400
When I graduated
as a kindergarten teacher,

15
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:53,800
being assigned to the Children's Palace

16
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:55,190
was quite an honor.

17
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:59,030
But I wasn't a teacher.

18
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:00,910
I worked in logistics.

19
00:03:03,150 --> 00:03:04,870
Back then, the people in our unit

20
00:03:04,870 --> 00:03:06,150
mostly got married and had kids

21
00:03:06,150 --> 00:03:07,560
in their twenties.

22
00:03:08,190 --> 00:03:10,390
So all of you kids
are about the same age.

23
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:14,280
When kids got together,

24
00:03:14,590 --> 00:03:16,190
it was all about comparing.

25
00:03:16,970 --> 00:03:18,250
I was young then

26
00:03:20,130 --> 00:03:21,340
and quite vain.

27
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:24,620
I already felt

28
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:26,410
inferior to the teachers,

29
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:29,940
and I was terrified you'd be outshined.

30
00:03:31,180 --> 00:03:32,440
Thinking about it now,

31
00:03:35,250 --> 00:03:37,250
I projected all my unfulfilled ambitions

32
00:03:37,250 --> 00:03:38,650
onto you.

33
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:46,020
Tingting.

34
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:51,590
You said several times earlier

35
00:03:52,930 --> 00:03:54,470
that you embarrassed me.

36
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:58,190
You embarrassed me.

37
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,700
I suddenly realized

38
00:04:04,310 --> 00:04:05,120
that I seem to

39
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:09,080
have never given you
any positive affirmation.

40
00:04:10,910 --> 00:04:11,370
But

41
00:04:12,310 --> 00:04:14,150
during the competition just now,

42
00:04:14,150 --> 00:04:16,310
I clearly felt so proud.

43
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:18,769
My daughter got into

44
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:21,920
the experimental class
of the best high school.

45
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:25,750
My daughter won second place
in the provincial competition.

46
00:04:25,750 --> 00:04:27,830
My daughter has accomplished
so many things

47
00:04:27,830 --> 00:04:30,270
that I could never possibly do.

48
00:04:31,430 --> 00:04:32,110
But why...

49
00:04:35,390 --> 00:04:37,870
why did I never tell her?

50
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,120
But I really did perform poorly today.

51
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:48,240
I didn't answer a single one
of my individual questions correctly.

52
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:50,830
I really envy Lin Zhixia.

53
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:54,750
She is the perfect child in adults' eyes.

54
00:04:54,870 --> 00:04:57,330
Her parents must be very proud of her,

55
00:04:57,330 --> 00:04:59,330
having such an excellent daughter.

56
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:00,620
Unlike me,

57
00:05:00,770 --> 00:05:02,860
who only disappoints you every time.

58
00:05:05,130 --> 00:05:05,930
Tingting.

59
00:05:10,220 --> 00:05:11,980
I am also very proud.

60
00:05:14,190 --> 00:05:18,060
I have always been proud of you.

61
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:20,060
Really?

62
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:23,320
Really.

63
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:26,980
You know what?

64
00:05:27,570 --> 00:05:29,450
In the competition just now,

65
00:05:30,220 --> 00:05:31,370
oh my goodness,

66
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:34,659
you were standing
with so many impressive people.

67
00:05:35,220 --> 00:05:36,659
I suddenly felt

68
00:05:38,420 --> 00:05:40,570
that my daughter has grown up.

69
00:05:42,060 --> 00:05:44,810
But I'm always stuck in the past,

70
00:05:44,810 --> 00:05:47,420
when you were following me around

71
00:05:47,420 --> 00:05:48,510
calling "Mom."

72
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:50,010
But

73
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:52,270
I don't know since when

74
00:05:54,690 --> 00:05:57,090
I've struggled to understand what you say.

75
00:05:58,620 --> 00:06:00,820
I also don't know what you like anymore.

76
00:06:02,770 --> 00:06:05,010
But the more I try to know your thoughts,

77
00:06:05,930 --> 00:06:07,620
the further you want to hide.

78
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:12,330
Tingting.

79
00:06:16,050 --> 00:06:17,810
I want to say sorry to you.

80
00:06:21,570 --> 00:06:23,930
I know my temper can be awful sometimes.

81
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:27,360
And what I say isn't pleasant to hear.

82
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:28,750
But...

83
00:06:30,060 --> 00:06:31,540
I was just worried.

84
00:06:32,980 --> 00:06:34,540
You came home,

85
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:36,450
shut your door,

86
00:06:36,890 --> 00:06:39,090
and even wore headphones while eating.

87
00:06:39,220 --> 00:06:41,130
I really had no choice.

88
00:06:41,740 --> 00:06:43,980
I could only talk to you

89
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:45,980
about your studies and your health.

90
00:06:48,180 --> 00:06:49,450
It's my fault.

91
00:06:52,370 --> 00:06:53,450
I have to learn

92
00:06:55,330 --> 00:06:56,060
to accept...

93
00:06:58,750 --> 00:06:59,570
to accept that my daughter

94
00:06:59,570 --> 00:07:01,500
is going to have her own world.

95
00:07:03,770 --> 00:07:06,620
Her world will get bigger and bigger,

96
00:07:08,660 --> 00:07:13,420
but I will get smaller and smaller in it.

97
00:07:17,620 --> 00:07:20,420
My baby will leave me sooner or later.

98
00:07:22,690 --> 00:07:24,220
I won't leave you.

99
00:07:27,130 --> 00:07:29,190
You won't leave even when you grow up?

100
00:07:29,810 --> 00:07:31,100
No.

101
00:07:32,100 --> 00:07:33,010
Okay.

102
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:36,770
You will always be my little baby.

103
00:07:38,620 --> 00:07:41,150
Even when I'm old,
I'll still be your old baby.

104
00:07:59,690 --> 00:08:00,260
[Congratulations to!]

105
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:01,640
[All contestants achieved
outstanding results in]

106
00:08:01,670 --> 00:08:02,920
[the Nanhai Rising Star Math Competition.
The list of winners is as follows:]

107
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:04,610
[First Prize]
[Jiang Yubai, Jin Baihui, Duan Qiyan]

108
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:06,660
[Second Prize]
[Lin Zhixia, Shen Fuxuan, Tang Tingting]

109
00:08:18,300 --> 00:08:19,100
Have you heard?

110
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:21,930
Lin Zhixia's team came in second
in the math competition.

111
00:08:21,930 --> 00:08:23,790
So even geniuses fail sometimes.

112
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:25,370
I watched that match.

113
00:08:25,420 --> 00:08:26,500
She was so arrogant,

114
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:28,230
only caring about showing off.

115
00:08:50,580 --> 00:08:52,580
Ladies and gentlemen,

116
00:08:52,580 --> 00:08:54,100
good morning!

117
00:08:54,890 --> 00:08:57,460
Here comes
the provincial first-prize winner.

118
00:08:57,460 --> 00:08:58,460
Don't call me that.

119
00:08:58,460 --> 00:09:00,620
It makes us sound like strangers.

120
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:01,820
If you ask me,

121
00:09:01,940 --> 00:09:03,980
Duan Qiyan didn't ride
his bike here today;

122
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:05,340
he floated here.

123
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:07,620
You're definitely right about that.

124
00:09:07,620 --> 00:09:10,280
My pockets haven't been this full
in a long time.

125
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:12,530
Your dad's mood

126
00:09:12,860 --> 00:09:14,220
is really unstable.

127
00:09:14,410 --> 00:09:15,580
What do you know?

128
00:09:15,940 --> 00:09:18,970
This is called being clear
about rewards and punishments.

129
00:09:18,970 --> 00:09:21,700
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

130
00:09:19,050 --> 00:09:22,100
I'm treating everyone
to McDonald's after school today.

131
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:23,530
Contestants

132
00:09:23,890 --> 00:09:25,100
and you guys

133
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:26,410
all have to come.

134
00:09:26,410 --> 00:09:28,640
-You hear me? Let's celebrate.
-Okay.

135
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:30,250
-I'm in.
-I'm in.

136
00:09:34,370 --> 00:09:36,170
Let's go together after school.

137
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:39,630
Alright.

138
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:47,620
Here comes the snack bucket.

139
00:09:51,050 --> 00:09:52,100
I ordered per person.

140
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:53,170
You guys eat first.

141
00:09:53,170 --> 00:09:54,770
If it's not enough,

142
00:09:54,770 --> 00:09:55,620
give me the coupons,

143
00:09:55,620 --> 00:09:56,740
and I'll order more for everyone.

144
00:09:56,740 --> 00:09:57,740
For today's meal,

145
00:09:57,980 --> 00:09:58,980
I'm paying.

146
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,170
That's awesome.

147
00:10:02,530 --> 00:10:04,220
You're really bleeding money today.

148
00:10:04,220 --> 00:10:05,890
This is fancier than the meal
you had for your birthday.

149
00:10:05,890 --> 00:10:06,890
Of course.

150
00:10:07,620 --> 00:10:10,170
This gathering for Class 1

151
00:10:10,170 --> 00:10:11,630
is of great significance.

152
00:10:11,860 --> 00:10:12,820
Why do I say that?

153
00:10:13,290 --> 00:10:14,340
Our school can be said to be

154
00:10:14,340 --> 00:10:16,980
the ever-victorious general
in this competition.

155
00:10:16,980 --> 00:10:19,530
The Provincial Experimental School
got first place in the preliminary.

156
00:10:19,530 --> 00:10:20,500
Did they really think

157
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:21,580
they could shake

158
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:23,170
our ruling position?

159
00:10:23,290 --> 00:10:24,340
How is that possible?

160
00:10:24,340 --> 00:10:25,770
Not to mention the championship,

161
00:10:25,770 --> 00:10:27,770
they didn't even get the runner-up.

162
00:10:28,050 --> 00:10:29,410
We are just too strong.

163
00:10:29,410 --> 00:10:31,890
Everyone, give us a round of applause!

164
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:33,160
-Come on.
-Come on.

165
00:10:37,580 --> 00:10:38,500
But to be honest,

166
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:40,620
the provincial first prize title
the three of you hold

167
00:10:40,620 --> 00:10:41,880
is still quite useful.

168
00:10:41,890 --> 00:10:43,250
Winning it in your freshman year

169
00:10:43,250 --> 00:10:44,370
means you can take
the independent recruitment exams

170
00:10:44,370 --> 00:10:45,620
of top universities

171
00:10:45,650 --> 00:10:48,580
in your sophomore and junior years.

172
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:51,440
You might even get
a recommendation for admission.

173
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:53,100
This has always been my goal.

174
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:55,140
It seems that hard work pays off.

175
00:10:55,530 --> 00:10:56,980
I don't expect a provincial first prize.

176
00:10:56,980 --> 00:10:58,220
The points I accumulated
for the second prize

177
00:10:58,220 --> 00:11:00,550
are enough to keep my mom
happy for months.

178
00:11:01,410 --> 00:11:02,220
In that case,

179
00:11:02,530 --> 00:11:03,820
let's all make a toast.

180
00:11:04,130 --> 00:11:05,860
To celebrate our best experimental class,

181
00:11:05,860 --> 00:11:07,820
sweeping the top two spots
in the competition.

182
00:11:07,820 --> 00:11:08,500
What do you say?

183
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:09,650
Come on, cheers!

184
00:11:10,250 --> 00:11:11,290
Don't forget,

185
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:12,580
we should also congratulate

186
00:11:12,580 --> 00:11:13,860
our best player.

187
00:11:14,050 --> 00:11:15,050
Yes, right.

188
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:18,130
Lin Zhixia is definitely the MVP,

189
00:11:18,130 --> 00:11:19,530
like a final boss.

190
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:20,860
Come on, let's toast!

191
00:11:20,860 --> 00:11:22,150
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

192
00:11:22,170 --> 00:11:24,650
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

193
00:11:27,700 --> 00:11:28,700
This is delicious.

194
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:29,530
Try this.

195
00:11:29,700 --> 00:11:30,500
Okay.

196
00:11:32,130 --> 00:11:33,190
Tissues. Tissues.

197
00:11:39,370 --> 00:11:40,390
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

198
00:11:40,390 --> 00:11:41,450
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

199
00:11:43,650 --> 00:11:44,850
-This one?
-Try this.

200
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:45,860
Which one? This?

201
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:48,050
-Yes.
-Do you want it? I'll eat it if you don't.

202
00:11:48,050 --> 00:11:48,980
I also want...

203
00:11:48,980 --> 00:11:49,580
What?

204
00:11:49,580 --> 00:11:50,170
A leg.

205
00:11:50,410 --> 00:11:51,340
If you don't eat it, I will.

206
00:11:51,340 --> 00:11:52,370
Seriously.

207
00:11:53,010 --> 00:11:54,470
You love eating that much?

208
00:11:55,010 --> 00:11:57,740
Duan Qiyan, you got lucky.

209
00:11:57,940 --> 00:11:59,250
Even though your grades
are better than ours,

210
00:11:59,250 --> 00:12:01,850
getting a provincial first prize
is a bit much.

211
00:12:02,010 --> 00:12:03,530
You do it if you can.

212
00:12:03,910 --> 00:12:05,050
Let me tell you,

213
00:12:05,170 --> 00:12:07,050
I was a top seed

214
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:09,960
that the champion
and runner-up teams fought over.

215
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:11,290
Are you okay?

216
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:13,250
I'm fine.

217
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:15,300
Am I invisible to you?

218
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:16,700
That's treason.

219
00:12:17,650 --> 00:12:19,010
Screw you. I don't care.

220
00:12:19,010 --> 00:12:20,220
I'm the champion anyway.

221
00:12:20,220 --> 00:12:21,130
Okay, okay.

222
00:12:21,130 --> 00:12:23,250
Since Mr. Duan is paying today,

223
00:12:23,250 --> 00:12:25,150
let's give the champion
a round of applause.

224
00:12:25,150 --> 00:12:25,960
Come on.

225
00:12:26,770 --> 00:12:29,100
Mr. Duan is always right today.

226
00:12:32,170 --> 00:12:34,700
I have something to do
at home. I'll get going.

227
00:12:35,460 --> 00:12:37,370
Okay, be careful on the road.

228
00:12:37,460 --> 00:12:38,990
See you on Monday. Bye-bye.

229
00:12:40,010 --> 00:12:41,340
Let's play basketball later.

230
00:12:41,340 --> 00:12:42,290
Definitely.

231
00:12:42,290 --> 00:12:43,370
I'll spot you one hand this time

232
00:12:43,370 --> 00:12:44,700
and see if you can score.

233
00:13:34,890 --> 00:13:35,500
Alright.

234
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:42,250
Your dad called this morning.

235
00:13:43,050 --> 00:13:46,650
He wanted to congratulate you

236
00:13:47,290 --> 00:13:48,940
for winning first place.

237
00:13:55,220 --> 00:13:57,410
I knew you wouldn't want to talk to him,

238
00:13:57,700 --> 00:13:59,430
so I told him you were sleeping.

239
00:14:03,940 --> 00:14:05,290
He must be bored.

240
00:14:05,980 --> 00:14:06,890
Doesn't he have anything to care about

241
00:14:06,890 --> 00:14:08,530
in his new family?

242
00:14:08,940 --> 00:14:10,980
His younger son can't even speak yet.

243
00:14:10,980 --> 00:14:13,780
Of course, he finds it easier
to interact with you.

244
00:14:13,890 --> 00:14:15,460
It's better not to talk.

245
00:14:15,890 --> 00:14:16,980
I am not sure

246
00:14:16,980 --> 00:14:18,440
what I might say to him now.

247
00:14:25,050 --> 00:14:25,860
I am

248
00:14:26,220 --> 00:14:28,130
not speaking for him.

249
00:14:29,010 --> 00:14:30,370
I just feel

250
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:32,580
that this whole blood tie thing

251
00:14:33,130 --> 00:14:34,390
is quite fascinating.

252
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:37,010
You know your dad.

253
00:14:37,290 --> 00:14:38,620
No one can handle him.

254
00:14:38,820 --> 00:14:40,250
But with you,

255
00:14:42,770 --> 00:14:44,580
he is really humble.

256
00:14:50,770 --> 00:14:52,460
He asked me to tell you

257
00:14:52,720 --> 00:14:53,650
that

258
00:14:53,860 --> 00:14:55,940
when you are in a good mood,

259
00:14:55,940 --> 00:14:57,460
give him a call,

260
00:14:57,890 --> 00:14:59,580
or a message is fine too.

261
00:15:01,530 --> 00:15:02,620
You have no idea.

262
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:04,410
Being a parent for the first time,

263
00:15:04,410 --> 00:15:06,100
the bond he shares with his child

264
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:07,340
can never be severed.

265
00:15:07,860 --> 00:15:08,700
So—

266
00:15:08,770 --> 00:15:10,230
Let's talk about it later.

267
00:15:20,010 --> 00:15:22,580
Why the long face?

268
00:15:23,620 --> 00:15:24,620
You got first place in the competition.

269
00:15:24,620 --> 00:15:26,050
Shouldn't you be happy?

270
00:16:45,170 --> 00:16:46,250
Hello.

271
00:16:47,890 --> 00:16:48,750
Hello, Auntie.

272
00:16:48,890 --> 00:16:50,220
I'm looking for Lin Zhixia.

273
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:51,280
I'm her classmate.

274
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:53,740
Zhixia is not home.

275
00:16:53,860 --> 00:16:54,890
She went out early in the morning

276
00:16:54,890 --> 00:16:56,340
and hasn't come back yet.

277
00:16:56,890 --> 00:16:57,980
What is your name?

278
00:16:57,980 --> 00:16:59,780
I'll tell her when she gets back.

279
00:17:02,620 --> 00:17:03,500
That's okay.

280
00:17:03,530 --> 00:17:05,180
It's nothing important.

281
00:17:05,660 --> 00:17:06,720
Thank you, Auntie.

282
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:19,220
Lin Zhixia.

283
00:17:23,050 --> 00:17:24,650
Time for school, Lin Zhixia.

284
00:17:24,770 --> 00:17:25,900
You are still in bed?

285
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:29,830
I took sick leave.

286
00:17:30,770 --> 00:17:32,630
Do I not know if you are sick or not?

287
00:17:33,940 --> 00:17:35,800
If you don't get up, I'm coming in.

288
00:17:38,850 --> 00:17:39,650
What's wrong?

289
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:42,460
I have a fever, Zeqiu.

290
00:17:42,530 --> 00:17:44,570
Remember to ask for sick leave for me.

291
00:17:44,570 --> 00:17:45,530
A fever?

292
00:17:49,770 --> 00:17:51,300
You are not even as hot as me.

293
00:17:52,250 --> 00:17:54,180
You just don't want to go to school.

294
00:17:56,570 --> 00:17:58,090
Leave me alone.

295
00:17:58,700 --> 00:18:00,420
Is it really necessary, Lin Zhixia?

296
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:03,550
It's just one competition
you didn't win first place in.

297
00:18:03,570 --> 00:18:05,250
What's the big deal?

298
00:18:06,090 --> 00:18:07,980
You just have never lost before.

299
00:18:07,980 --> 00:18:10,180
You can't even handle a little setback.

300
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:11,010
In this world,

301
00:18:11,010 --> 00:18:13,140
